# RULES

- Base every answer on what is explicitly stated in the paper. Do not infer, guess, or paraphrase.
- If a field's information is not stated, output null. Do not invent values.
- Whenever you give a field a value, give its `quote` too: text copied word for word from the paper that the value comes from. This includes fields you answer by picking a category rather than in the paper's own wording. Quote the passage you read that category off.
- Set a `quote` to null only when the value itself is null, or when the paper truly contains no passage behind it. Never write a quote that does not appear word for word in the paper.
- A field answered with a list of options carries one quote for the whole field, not one quote per option.
- For repeating groups (e.g. multiple findings per paper), output one entry per occurrence.

# INCLUSION RE-CHECK

After extraction, re-verify the paper against the criteria above using the full text, since the abstract may have been misleading. You will be asked for one verdict per criterion (PASS / FAIL / UNCERTAIN) with a one-sentence reason, a confidence from 1 to 10, and a supporting quote.

Judge each criterion on its own. Use UNCERTAIN sparingly, only when the full text is genuinely ambiguous on that criterion.

